The Clearing
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/the_lodge]

FIXME(dread): Deep on the trail, you come upon a man dragged up against a deadfall log, badly mauled. One thigh is torn open and the leg below it crushed; a slow bleed, hours from death. His breathing is ragged and desperate. He is perhaps forty, salt-and-pepper hair, short-cropped beard. He wears hunter's leathers; a tracker or scout. Someone familiar with the forest. You know these wounds. You have taken smaller ones from the same jaws.

FIXME(dread): The wounded man has not seen you yet. Across the clearing you catch a glimpse of the beast, low and quick between the trunks, farther away each moment. It is not fleeing. It is keeping ahead of you.

choices:

* Stop and help = Perhaps you can save the man's life [requires has medical_kit]
    FIXME(mundane): The man stares at you wild-eyed. "Leave me," he says. "You'll lose it. Kill it. Carry my revenge to it." You ignore the cries; the bleeding must be dealt with first. You drop your pack and fetch your medical kit.
    @if check Bushcraft correct:bind wrong:probe {
        FIXME(mundane): You bind the thigh hard above the wound and splint the crushed leg. The man howls with pain, then breathes easier. You can't do much for the pain, but the bleeding slows to a seep. "Enough," the man says. "Go, go, this is not the worst hurt I've suffered; I'll see after myself." You nod, shove everything back in your pack, and head in the direction you last saw the beast.
        FIXME(mundane): Toward dusk you hear singing, light and airy, in the distance. You follow it to a small clearing: a cabin, a garden, a fenced run of chickens. The woman there falls silent when she sees you, then calls a greeting. When she hears how far you mean to go, she offers her loft for the night. "Full dark in near an hour. You can take the bed if you like, I sleep on the chair, helps my back."
        +open "Yana"
    } @else {
        FIXME(mundane): The wound is worse than it looks, and it looks bad. The bleeding will not stop. By the time you have it under control, the man is unconscious and the light is failing. You consider leaving him, but he'd not survive the night this far into the woods.
        FIXME(mundane): He awakens a few hours later. Says his name is Simon. Thanks you for saving him. Says his sister wandered into these woods some three months back; what was found of her was in a pitiful state. Folk blamed a beast that lives in the deep forest and kills those who come here. He's been hunting it since. Today it stopped running and came back for him.
        FIXME(dread): In time, night falls. You scout for the beast's trail, find signs of its passing but nothing you can follow in the dark, and return to camp. Simon is gone. You call his name into the dark, but there is no answer. You sleep in fits and starts, your dreams plagued by the beast and Simon's screams. In the morning, you try to pick up Simon's trail, but to no end. It seems he stumbled into the woods a dozen yards, then vanished. You return to the road. Whatever was happening here, it's lost to you now.
        +finish_dungeon
    }


* End his suffering = Give him a clean death
    FIXME(dread): The man stares at you, uncertain. As you draw your knife, recognition passes over his face. He nods and closes his eyes. As you do the work, his final words are simply "Annabelle." You wipe your blade and go after the beast.
    FIXME(mundane): You head deeper into the forest, always just out of sight of your prey. Yet each time you think you've lost the path, you notice something small. A broken branch. A stone pushed into the mud. The shadow of a footprint.
    FIXME(mundane): You hear singing, light and airy, in the distance. A strange foreign sound this deep in the wood. You follow it and come upon a small clearing. There is a woman here; she falls silent when she sees you. "Oh, you gave me a scare. Not polite to sneak up on folk. Not many visitors out here." She's maybe 30, short-cropped blonde hair. Linen dress with a leather apron.
    FIXME(mundane): She has a small cabin here, a little smoker off to one side, garden on another. There's a small fenced-off area with chickens. She calls out before you are close enough that she needs to raise her voice. Asks where you've come from. Listens to whatever you tell her without much reaction. After a moment she sets the axe against the stump.
    "Full dark in near an hour. You can take the bed if you like, I sleep on the chair, helps my back."
    +open "Yana"

* Press on with your pursuit = You have no time for mercy
    FIXME(mundane): You press on with your pursuit. For all you know, the man was left in your path to slow you down.
    FIXME(mundane): The trail leads you on until dusk, when you hear singing in the distance and follow it to a small clearing: a cabin, a garden, a fenced run of chickens. The woman there falls silent when she sees you, then calls a greeting. With full dark an hour off, she offers her loft for the night. "You can take the bed if you like, I sleep on the chair, helps my back."
    +open "Yana"
